## User preferences

- For creator copy, use only stated motivation, ask "短い質問を原則1つずつ", and do not add a motivation/story the user has not said. [Task 1] [ad-hoc note]
- Treat voice-input breaks or odd wording as unconfirmed: ask rather than silently correcting "作りまし……" or "木にする". [Task 1]
- The user's framing is rehearsal/workflow efficiency that creates time for through-runs and confident practice toward a better show, not a generic story about helping "困っている人". [Task 1]
- Two work orders must run in the specified order as separate waves/commits; derive the later cache version from live `index.html`, not the order's stale value. Push is prohibited. [Task 2]
- Overnight work must stop at local commits: no push, publication, deployment, external sending, or deletion. [Task 2]

## Reusable knowledge

- Keep interview source-of-truth in `obsidian-vault/ideas/2026-07-28_舞台スケッチとルーティンノート_このアプリについて.md`, separating spoken text, confirmed core, unconfirmed points, and the next one-question prompt. Do not put raw interview records in public `shosai-app/`. [Task 1]
- Stage Sketch arose from a need to see direction, team communication, role/position/freedom, and audience/director view with an overhead plan; the approved Japanese copy is about 1,000 characters and English uses natural stage-production terms: `Stage Sketch`, `About This App`, `plan view`, `front view`, `Developer`. It is a communication/practice sketch, not a technical drawing or safety guarantee. [Task 1]
- Wave 1 commit `f18f14fd7f42dd7f68aacdc8ba5d9736cc66078d` added 10 beat templates, treating #2休憩 as a normal scene with English support. Wave 2 `909d9816b847803004b510d780d7d5284ee4a536` added the About modal and two entry points; cache refs are style 124 / i18n 36 / sketch 175 / db 79. Tests 18/18, MCP 7/7, syntax, page parity, duplicate TEXT keys, and ledger final validation passed. [Task 2]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Workspace root is not Git; run Git checks from `show-creative-ideas/shosai-app`. Protected dirty `README.md` and `docs/IPAD_DEVICE_TEST.md` remained byte-identical and excluded from both commits. [Task 1][Task 2]
- The modal backdrop click was not independently replayed because the available browser locator could not target outside the centered modal; event wiring and its focused registration test passed, so retain this limitation rather than claiming full UI verification. [Task 2]

